I have a pre-quest Monk with the following stats:

Byron the Student of Stones     
St:25 Dx:17 Co:18 In:12 Wi:18 Ch:15  Neutral
Dlvl:14 $:0  HP:80(80) Pw:74(74) AC:-9 Xp:12/28933 T:26345

I'm in solid mid-game mode. I've finished the Mines, Sokoban,
and the Big Room. As you can see I'm not yet up to taking on the
Quest. In addition to the normal Monk instrinsics for 12th level
I have access to the following:

1) MR in the form of +4 MagicBane (god gift) and a couple of cloaks
of MR.

2) 2 amulets of reflection.

3) Multiple magic markers and I know charging.

4) Invisibility

5) Multiple BoHs with the primary one blessed up.

6) More holy water than I can carry.

7) Slow digestion! Yeah!

8) misc items such as water breathing, levitation, digging
and the like.

So as you can see it's a pretty good game. And I haven't yet
enchanted up everything.

This is the first Monk I've taken this deep into midgame. So here's my
dilimma:  g - a wand of wishing (0:1)

I found it in a bones pile. So I have 5 wishes I can utilize at a
pre-quest, pre-Castle stage.

But I'm really not sure what to do with them. For normal characters I'd start
with GDSM/SDSM, magic markers, and speed boots. If I have a neutral
character, I'd usually even consider the Eyes of the Overworld. But with this
Monk other than the speed boots, I'm set.

Of course a wish could go to a Helm of Brilliance. Monks can
get to decent spellcasting abilities, and I can definitely see a
HoB/robe combo as useful as I progress deeper into the game.

One site suggests that The Eye of the Aethiopica may be a good choice
because it confers MR when carried, so it can substitute for GDSM
which are virtually useless for Monks.

So even if I use two wishes for these two useful items, I'd still have 3 left
to apply for other stuff. I just wanted to get some thoughts because this
Monk looks like he may have the goods to go all the way. I also figure I
can't screw up too badly because I still can look forward to the Castle WoW
to finish kitting up for Gehennom and a final Ascension Run.

So tell me what your shopping list would be.

